                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers[/h1]\n\nYou can watch my full gameplay & review here: https://youtu.be/BEV0encrTrg\n\nI believe i got this game in a VR bundle for about .50 cents and that would be about the right price for this game. It's nowhere near being worth $4.99 USD. You can finish the whole game in about 2 minutes. You can replay the game, but it would be about the same experience.\n\nIn this game, you basically pick either a Pug, Corgi, or Lab puppy. Then you decide which of a few outfit choices to pick for your puppy and put perfume on it for reasons unknown. Then you take a photo. Then you play fetch with a frisbee with your puppy (a clunky mini-game of frisbee). Then it's game over, back to main menu.\n\nThis game came out in November 2017 in Early Access and it's been abandoned. There have been zero updates. Don't get me wrong, this game is super cute. I imagine small kids would love this game .... for 2-10 minutes. Is that worth $5? Not to me and I love Pugs. This game is more like a demo than anything else.\n\n[b]Rate 4/10. If you can find it for .50 cents or less, then I could say it's worth it. Otherwise, avoid.[/b]",
